4. System packages in the Docker images
---------------------------------------

The images are based on the official node:22-alpine (Dockerfile) and
node:22-bookworm-slim (Dockerfile.voip) images and install, from the distribution's
package repositories:

- ffmpeg: licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later, or GPL-2.0-or-later when built with GPL
  components, as distribution packages commonly are. Used as an external program to
  transcode voice notes and to generate the test tone of voice calls.
- tini: MIT.
- ca-certificates (Dockerfile.voip only): MPL-2.0 / GPL-2.0-or-later.

Their licenses are shipped inside the images by the distribution packages.

The stand-alone docker-compose.yml of qr-service/ also references the image postgres:16-alpine (service
zapo-db): PostgreSQL License for Postgres, several licenses for the Alpine packages. It is only referenced by
name and tag, not redistributed.


5. Native and WebAssembly components of the voice-call stack
------------------------------------------------------------

- @roamhq/wrtc 0.10.0 (BSD-2-Clause): prebuilt WebRTC binary, loaded only when
  VOIP_ENABLED=1.
- @zapo-js/voip 1.1.0, libmlow-wasm 0.1.1 (MIT).


To list the license of every installed package yourself, from qr-service/:

  npx license-checker --production --summary
